course: dictionary
lesson: 431
title: Arachnids are not insects
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An arachnid is a small animal with eight legs and a body in two main parts. Spiders, scorpions, ticks and mites are all arachnids.
explain: Arachnids are not insects. Counting legs is a quick check: «Spiders have eight legs and two body parts, insects have six legs and three body parts.»
explain: Some arachnids can bite or sting, so be careful around them. Never touch an animal you do not know, even a small one.
fact: An arachnid has eight legs. An insect has six.
fact: «Spiders are arachnids, together with scorpions, ticks and mites.»
fact: The harvestman, or daddy longlegs, is an arachnid but not a spider.
fact: «Arachnid» can be a noun (an arachnid, arachnids) or an adjective (arachnid).
fact: In a science lesson, you can use leg counts to sort animals into arachnids and insects.
exercise: How many legs does an arachnid have? | Six | Ten | Four | *Eight
exercise: Which of these is an arachnid? | A bee | *A tick | A beetle | A butterfly
exercise: Which statement is true? | Spiders are insects with six legs | Insects have eight legs | *Arachnids are not insects | Arachnids are insects
test: Is a scorpion an arachnid? | No, it is an insect | Only if it has wings | Only if it is a spider | *Yes
test: According to «Spiders have eight legs and two body parts», how many body parts do spiders have? | *Two | Three | Eight | Six
exam: «The harvestman, or daddy longlegs, is an arachnid but not a spider.» What does this tell you? | *Arachnid is a group bigger than spiders | Arachnids are always insects | All arachnids spin silk | Harvestmen are spiders
